      "seed": 430099653,
      "version": 44,
      "versionNonce": 1569678469,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788289755845,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose: RAM = 8 GB\nAnd we run:\n\nProcess A = 4 GB\nProcess B = 4 GB\nProcess C = 4 GB\n\nThat's: 12 GB requested\n\nBut we only have:  8 GB physical RAM\n\nDoes Linux immediately say: \"Impossible!\"\n\nNot necessarily.\n\nThis is where virtual memory, demand paging, page cache, swap, and eventually the \nOOM killer come into play.\nWe'll get to that.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose: RAM = 8 GB\nAnd we run:\n\nProcess A = 4 GB\nProcess B = 4 GB\nProcess C = 4 GB\n\nThat's: 12 GB requested\n\nBut we only have:  8 GB physical RAM\n\nDoes Linux immediately say: \"Impossible!\"\n\nNot necessarily.\n\nThis is where virtual memory, demand paging, page cache, swap, and eventually the \nOOM killer come into play.\nWe'll get to that.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xSyxddYDaBy19VvibLlIX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 667.5637146898734,
      "y": 10035.399331063432,
      "width": 187,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4s",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 750425765,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1160608965,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788289789712,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "7. Process Memory",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "7. Process Memory",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YXDNGpG7HlTyGLC4WtwHI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 715.5637146898734,
      "y": 10060.274331063432,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 696939077,
      "version": 22,
      "versionNonce": 121571819,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788289871433,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A running process doesn't just have one giant block of memory.\nConceptually, its virtual address space contains regions such as:\n\nHigh Address\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│       Stack         │\n│         ↓           │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│                     │\n│       ...           │\n│                     │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│         ↑           │\n│       Heap          │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│ BSS                 │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│ Data                │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│ Code / Text         │\n└─────────────────────┘\nLow Address\n\nwe don't need to memorize the exact layout yet.\n\nThe important parts for us are:\nCode\nData\nHeap\nStack\nLet's understand them.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A running process doesn't just have one giant block of memory.\nConceptually, its virtual address space contains regions such as:\n\nHigh Address\n┌─────────────────────┐\n│       Stack         │\n│         ↓           │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│                     │\n│       ...           │\n│                     │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│         ↑           │\n│       Heap          │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│ BSS                 │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│ Data                │\n├─────────────────────┤\n│ Code / Text         │\n└─────────────────────┘\nLow Address\n\nwe don't need to memorize the exact layout yet.\n\nThe important parts for us are:\nCode\nData\nHeap\nStack\nLet's understand them.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hwfKjvdIp9WrMg4oqkHYh",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 668.5637146898734,
      "y": 10916.399331063432,
      "width": 242,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2066196581,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 267839109,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788289973480,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "8. Code / Text Segment",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "8. Code / Text Segment",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CuCp7b8XKLXjOPB68IwnC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 702.5637146898734,
      "y": 10951.153237313432,
      "width": 1012,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2044833835,
      "version": 23,
      "versionNonce": 1738167979,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290034544,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose:\n\ndef calculate():\n    return 10 + 20\n\nThe instructions needed to execute the program live in the program's code/text segment.\n\nConceptually:\n\nPython Process\n      |\n      ├── Code\n      ├── Data\n      ├── Heap\n      └── Stack\n\nThe code is generally read-only while executing.\nWhy?\nBecause you don't want random code execution paths modifying the application's instructions.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose:\n\ndef calculate():\n    return 10 + 20\n\nThe instructions needed to execute the program live in the program's code/text segment.\n\nConceptually:\n\nPython Process\n      |\n      ├── Code\n      ├── Data\n      ├── Heap\n      └── Stack\n\nThe code is generally read-only while executing.\nWhy?\nBecause you don't want random code execution paths modifying the application's instructions.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9RvY2sFnXuiL6kiBmHG8L",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 668.5637146898734,
      "y": 11521.399331063432,
      "width": 88,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 163623563,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1109531243,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290047214,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "9. Stack",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "9. Stack",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "j1pIKx7CbpGjfh_Wk50bB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 696.5637146898734,
      "y": 11552.395424813432,
      "width": 693,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1922895845,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 369981509,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290141273,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The stack is used for function calls and local execution state.\nConsider:\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    result = a + b\n    return result\n\nadd(10, 20)\n\nWhen add() executes, the process needs information such as:\n\na\nb\nresult\nreturn information\n\nThe stack helps manage this function-call information.\n\nConceptually:\n\nmain()\n |\n └── add()\n      |\n      ├── a\n      ├── b\n      ├── result\n      └── return address\n\nadd()\nWhen the function finishes: its stack frame can be removed.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The stack is used for function calls and local execution state.\nConsider:\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    result = a + b\n    return result\n\nadd(10, 20)\n\nWhen add() executes, the process needs information such as:\n\na\nb\nresult\nreturn information\n\nThe stack helps manage this function-call information.\n\nConceptually:\n\nmain()\n |\n └── add()\n      |\n      ├── a\n      ├── b\n      ├── result\n      └── return address\n\nadd()\nWhen the function finishes: its stack frame can be removed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SDP73MQSHZklx2iwN3JGL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 654.5637146898734,
      "y": 12415.399331063432,
      "width": 88,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4z",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1965539851,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1507416555,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290202491,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "10. Heap",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "10. Heap",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FhWT7vT-oBzGXeIjz-lac",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 688.2121521898734,
      "y": 12455.422768563432,
      "width": 891,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b50",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1691900005,
      "version": 94,
      "versionNonce": 355455813,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290297825,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The heap is used for dynamically allocated memory.\nPython makes heavy use of dynamic memory.\nFor example:\n\nusers = []\n\nThen:\n\nusers.append(\"Amit\")\nusers.append(\"Rahul\")\nusers.append(\"Rishabh\")\n\nObjects created during execution require memory.\nConceptually:\n\nHeap\n│\n├── Python objects\n├── Lists\n├── Dictionaries\n├── Strings\n├── Django objects\n└── Other dynamically allocated data\n\nThis is why a Python application's memory usage can grow significantly depending \non what objects it keeps alive.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The heap is used for dynamically allocated memory.\nPython makes heavy use of dynamic memory.\nFor example:\n\nusers = []\n\nThen:\n\nusers.append(\"Amit\")\nusers.append(\"Rahul\")\nusers.append(\"Rishabh\")\n\nObjects created during execution require memory.\nConceptually:\n\nHeap\n│\n├── Python objects\n├── Lists\n├── Dictionaries\n├── Strings\n├── Django objects\n└── Other dynamically allocated data\n\nThis is why a Python application's memory usage can grow significantly depending \non what objects it keeps alive.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GGsPqy_3X9Z37GxbgRakF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 648.5637146898734,
      "y": 13182.399331063432,
      "width": 187,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b52",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1396211045,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 819714949,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290318709,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "11. Stack vs Heap",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "11. Stack vs Heap",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yQhZWZINMeFZ_GaFEjkJ1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 696.4348084398734,
      "y": 13211.399331063432,
      "width": 1133,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b53",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2046585643,
      "version": 15,
      "versionNonce": 254658475,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290371328,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This is a common interview topic.\n\n| Stack                                     | Heap                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| Function-call information                 | Dynamically allocated objects           |\n| Usually smaller                           | Usually much larger                     |\n| Automatically managed as calls return     | Objects remain until released/reclaimed |\n| Very fast access                          | More flexible                           |\n| Stores stack frames/local execution state | Stores dynamically created data         |\n\n\nFor Python specifically, don't overgeneralize the C/C++ model: Python objects themselves generally \nlive in heap-managed memory, while the Python interpreter uses its own structures for execution frames.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This is a common interview topic.\n\n| Stack                                     | Heap                                    |\n| ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| Function-call information                 | Dynamically allocated objects           |\n| Usually smaller                           | Usually much larger                     |\n| Automatically managed as calls return     | Objects remain until released/reclaimed |\n| Very fast access                          | More flexible                           |\n| Stores stack frames/local execution state | Stores dynamically created data         |\n\n\nFor Python specifically, don't overgeneralize the C/C++ model: Python objects themselves generally \nlive in heap-managed memory, while the Python interpreter uses its own structures for execution frames.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SupHFJgaZoSR2UneJGvq2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 650.5637146898734,
      "y": 13615.399331063432,
      "width": 352,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b54",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 459129739,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 179096427,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290379642,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "12. Let's Connect This to Django",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "12. Let's Connect This to Django",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "8zirt_3eQF9_KZdtRtCXx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 683.5637146898734,
      "y": 13652.399331063432,
      "width": 583,
      "height": 850,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b55",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 287910469,
      "version": 25,
      "versionNonce": 318716619,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788290517819,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose you have:\n\nDjango\n |\n ├── Python interpreter\n ├── Django framework\n ├── Imported libraries\n ├── Database connection objects\n ├── Request objects\n ├── Query results\n └── Application objects\n\nAll of these consume memory.\nImagine your API does:\n\nusers = User.objects.all()\n\nand then loads a huge number of objects into memory.\nYou could suddenly have:\n\nDjango Worker\n\nRAM usage\n   ↑\n   |\n   |       █\n   |      ██\n   |     ███\n   |    ████\n   |   █████\n   +----------------> time\n\nThis becomes important later when we discuss:\nGunicorn workers + Docker + Kubernetes memory limits.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose you have:\n\nDjango\n |\n ├── Python interpreter\n ├── Django framework\n ├── Imported libraries\n ├── Database connection objects\n ├── Request objects\n ├── Query results\n └── Application objects\n\nAll of these consume memory.\nImagine your API does:\n\nusers = User.objects.all()\n\nand then loads a huge number of objects into memory.\nYou could suddenly have:\n\nDjango Worker\n\nRAM usage\n   ↑\n   |\n   |       █\n   |      ██\n   |     ███\n   |    ████\n   |   █████\n   +----------------> time\n\nThis becomes important later when we discuss:\nGunicorn workers + Docker + Kubernetes memory limits.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kJHf6mheoyDIe6fDpTQuL",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 638.5637146898734,
      "y": 14568.399331063432,
      "width": 209,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b56",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1529228357,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1816229477,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788291180564,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "13. What is a Page?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "13. What is a Page?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "pL2OO-2E0UeH-V25P0CBv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 684.5637146898734,
      "y": 14605.883706063432,
      "width": 737,
      "height": 700,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b57",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1418183243,
      "version": 35,
      "versionNonce": 458327339,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788291260930,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Linux doesn't normally manage memory as one giant continuous chunk.\nMemory is divided into fixed-size pieces called pages.\nA common page size is: 4 KB\n\nSo instead of thinking: Process needs 100 MB\n\nthe OS can think:\n\nPage\nPage\nPage\nPage\nPage\n...\n\nThe virtual memory system maps these pages to physical memory.\n\nConceptually:\n\nVirtual Memory\n\nPage 1 ──────────┐\nPage 2 ──────────┤\nPage 3 ──────────┼──> Physical RAM\nPage 4 ──────────┤\nPage 5 ──────────┘\n\nThis page-based system is fundamental to Linux memory management.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Linux doesn't normally manage memory as one giant continuous chunk.\nMemory is divided into fixed-size pieces called pages.\nA common page size is: 4 KB\n\nSo instead of thinking: Process needs 100 MB\n\nthe OS can think:\n\nPage\nPage\nPage\nPage\nPage\n...\n\nThe virtual memory system maps these pages to physical memory.\n\nConceptually:\n\nVirtual Memory\n\nPage 1 ──────────┐\nPage 2 ──────────┤\nPage 3 ──────────┼──> Physical RAM\nPage 4 ──────────┤\nPage 5 ──────────┘\n\nThis page-based system is fundamental to Linux memory management.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yW4UJmAVbbp_zM4o-k7sl",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 612.5637146898734,
      "y": 15356.399331063432,
      "width": 539,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b58",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1504211211,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1866754283,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788291268116,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "14. Why Pages Are Important for Docker/Kubernetes",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "14. Why Pages Are Important for Docker/Kubernetes",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EYpCYY4zTYSBiXuS3f9xi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 649.5637146898734,
      "y": 15388.278237313432,
      "width": 891,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b59",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 473520485,
      "version": 19,
      "versionNonce": 83134987,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788291307045,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Later we'll configure something like:\n\nresources:\n  limits:\n    memory: \"512Mi\"\n\nKubernetes isn't magically giving your application exactly 512 MB of special RAM.\nIt is enforcing a memory resource limit through Linux's underlying mechanisms.\nEventually we'll connect:\n\nKubernetes\n     ↓\nContainer\n     ↓\nLinux cgroups\n     ↓\nMemory accounting/limits\n     ↓\nPhysical memory\n\nSo understanding Linux memory first makes Kubernetes much easier.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Later we'll configure something like:\n\nresources:\n  limits:\n    memory: \"512Mi\"\n\nKubernetes isn't magically giving your application exactly 512 MB of special RAM.\nIt is enforcing a memory resource limit through Linux's underlying mechanisms.\nEventually we'll connect:\n\nKubernetes\n     ↓\nContainer\n     ↓\nLinux cgroups\n     ↓\nMemory accounting/limits\n     ↓\nPhysical memory\n\nSo understanding Linux memory first makes Kubernetes much easier.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iUbRx7hGUfV4gWg9Kb6-m",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 603.5637146898734,
      "y": 15967.399331063432,
      "width": 319,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
